  "limitations": [
    "A unique parcel's full polygon is checked against zoning and future land-use layers when valid geometry is available. Intersections include boundary touches; multiple designations require agency review and do not by themselves prove split zoning.",
    "Direct property layers cover Tampa, St. Petersburg, Clearwater and Pasco County. Pasco county land-use layers are used only after municipal boundaries exclude incorporated cities.",
    "Address labels do not establish jurisdiction; authoritative boundary polygons choose land-use sources.",
    "An unavailable, ambiguous or oversized parcel geometry falls back to a clearly identified address-point check. Whole-parcel intersections are bounded and source truncation remains explicit.",
    "A layer designation is not a development entitlement, approval, or official zoning determination.",
    "Layer update timestamps may describe one feature rather than the currency of the entire dataset."
  ],
